From 423e36d548c2d87143f1671c3dc6e7093728782c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mingyang Sun (Public)" <Mingyang.Sun@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:36:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] fix(clr): don't take the gfx1250 OCP builtin path on
 gfx1250-strict

gfx1250-strict does not have the block16 convert ops. LLVM commit
75f35e17f755 ("[AMDGPU] Disable block16 conversions on gfx1250-strict",
#222597) therefore gates the fp4/fp6 -> f16/bf16/f32 unpack builtins behind
"block16-cvt-scale-insts", which FeatureISAVersion12_50_STRICT omits:

  error: '__builtin_amdgcn_cvt_scale_pk8_f16_fp4' needs target feature
         block16-cvt-scale-insts

That compiler behaviour is correct and is not what this change addresses.

#11551 added __gfx1250_strict__ to HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS, which
routes gfx1250-strict into the hardware-builtin branches. Those branches
guard each call with __builtin_amdgcn_is_invocable() but have no else, so on
gfx1250-strict the guard correctly evaluates false and the zero-initialized
destination is returned unchanged: the conversion silently yields 0. The
software path that already exists as the preprocessor #else is unreachable
while the macro is 1.

Restore the pre-#11551 definition of HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS so
gfx1250-strict takes the existing fcbx software path, as it did before. No
conversion logic is added or duplicated, and this covers every site gated by
the macro across amd_hip_fp4.h, amd_hip_fp6.h and amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp rather
than only the ones a per-call-site audit happens to catch.

#11551's purpose is unaffected: amd_hip_fp8.h tests
(__gfx1250__ || __gfx1250_strict__) directly rather than via this macro, so
FP8 keeps using native conversions on gfx1250-strict.

Before the gfx1250-strict target existed these conversions were covered by
the rocjitsu hotswap translator, which was enabled by default. With hotswap
now opt-in and off by default nothing covers them, so the emulation moves
back into the header.

Measured on gfx1250-strict:

  fp4 roundtrip  9/10 mismatches -> 0/10
  fp6 roundtrip  7/8  mismatches -> 0/8
  fp8            v_cvt_f32_fp8_e32 / v_cvt_pk_fp8_f32, unchanged
  gfx1250        v_cvt_scale_pk8_f32_fp4 / v_cvt_scalef32_pk8_fp4_f32,
                 unchanged

Note FP4/FP6 conversion is software-emulated on gfx1250-strict, which has no
hardware unpack for these formats, so MX performance there is not
representative of gfx1250.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4f32467dd30bfc1c5d42d9de81e0e74d1497dc17)
---
 .../clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h     | 4 ++--
 projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h b/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h
index 82eba78f..e2d74d87 100644
--- a/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h
+++ b/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h
@@ -10,12 +10,12 @@
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX950_OCP_BUILTINS 0
 #endif
-#if defined(__gfx1250__) || defined(__gfx1250_strict__)
+#if defined(__gfx1250__)
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS 1
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS 0
 #endif
-#if !defined(__gfx950__) && !defined(__gfx1250__) && !defined(__gfx1250_strict__)
+#if !defined(__gfx950__) && !defined(__gfx1250__)
 #define HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS 1
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS 0
diff --git a/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp b/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp
index 54fe59bf..5b199c27 100644
--- a/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp
+++ b/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp
@@ -30,12 +30,12 @@ static_assert(sizeof(__hip_uint64_t) * CHAR_BIT == 64);
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX950_OCP_BUILTINS 0
 #endif
-#if defined(__gfx1250__) || defined(__gfx1250_strict__)
+#if defined(__gfx1250__)
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS 1
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS 0
 #endif
-#if !defined(__gfx950__) and !defined(__gfx1250__) and !defined(__gfx1250_strict__)
+#if !defined(__gfx950__) and !defined(__gfx1250__)
 #define HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS 1
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS 0
